> it is a kind of python library used for configuration management
> control plane and many target machines
> installation (apt/pip) refer official documentation 
> https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/latest/installation_guide/installation_distros.html#installing-ansible-on-ubuntu
> allow 22 from control plane sg (on every terget machines)
> to turn of host_key_checking 
  > /etc/ansible/ansible.cfg  copy the command for including plugins and run from cd /etc/ansible#
  > host_key_checking=False

> difference between ansible task: and handlers:
  > task runs every time
  > handlers run only if there is any conifuration change occure 
    #Purpose: Run a task only when notified (typically after a change).
    #Use Case: Restarting a service only if a config file was updated.
    #Example: notify: restart nginx after changing a config.

> use of template module
    #Purpose: Dynamically generate configuration files using Jinja2 templates.
    #Use Case: When you need to insert variables (like IPs, usernames) into config files.
    #Example: Creating nginx.conf with values from Ansible variables.
    
      

